   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜と思います: my opinion",
     "texto": [
      "To give your opinion, put the sentence in the plain form and add **と おもいます** (I think that…): **にほんご は むずかしい と おもいます** (I think Japanese is difficult).",
      "This is the usual way of giving an opinion. To ask someone's opinion you say **どう おもいます か** (what do you think?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜でしょう: probability or confirmation",
     "texto": [
      "**でしょう** expresses an assumption: **きょう は さむい でしょう** (it's probably cold today). With a rising intonation it can ask for confirmation: **きょう は さむい でしょう？** (it's cold today, isn't it?). **たぶん** means «probably» and makes the uncertainty explicit: **たぶん あした は あめ でしょう**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
